WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.520
When I came back to LSU,

2
00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:09.820
I lived [in the house] as an instructor for a number of years and the boys came back from the war.

3
00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:14.320
Girls were getting married and we did not have married students before this,

4
00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:20.260
you see, until after the war and then you had couples on the campus.

5
00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:26.120
And it was difficult to say to them . . . This was the requirement for all home economics majors at that time,

6
00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:29.980
to live in a home management residence.

7
00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:30.980
And it was difficult to say to them, you know,

8
00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:36.260
“You’ve got to leave your husband for nine weeks and come live in this home management house situation.”

9
00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:45.160
So we were beginning to realize that this was not the best way to handle teaching home management.

10
00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:49.360
It was an excellent way, but it was not practical.

11
00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:58.920
We started experimenting and I remember Elizabeth Tucker had a group of couples that lived in the Morris House,

12
00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:02.200
three couples . . . The boys just agreed to do it.

13
00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:09.700
They didn’t get any credit for it, but they agreed to assume responsibility to see what, you know, what it was like.

14
00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:15.240
And it was an interesting experience to have men doing these household jobs,

15
00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:19.600
because they looked at it, they approached it from a completely different point of view.

16
00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:28.660
I’ll never forget the day I walked in the kitchen one day and here was this boy drying (we didn’t have dishwashers then),

17
00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:36.966
drying the dishes, and he had a dishtowel and then he’d put all the silver in the dishtowel and rolled it up and just shook it.

18
00:01:36.966 --> 00:01:39.860
“Oh, this is a quicker way to dry those forks and knives.”

19
00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:41.340
And I was like, “Well, that’s pretty good!”
